{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014GymtWVZX7dSvBgqTMBXiM","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Perfect! I found the answer. Based on the context filesystem, here's the answer to your question:\\\\n\\\\n## Answer\\\\n\\\\nIn the proposal about **KIP-1262: Enable auto-formatting directories** (which allows brokers and observer controllers to skip storage formatting before startup), the cluster ID field in the new **ClusterIdRecord** metadata record used to persist the cluster ID in the log is defined as type **String**.\\\\n\\\\nAs documented in the discussion:\\\\n\\\\n> **JR1 (ClusterIdRecord type)**: Explains rationale for keeping UUID as String to support existing clusters with non-UUID cluster IDs during MV upgrades\\\\n\\\\nThis design decision keeps the cluster ID as a String type (rather than a stricter UUID type) to support backward compatibility with existing clusters that might have non-UUID cluster IDs when they undergo metadata version upgrades.\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/discussions.md` - Lines 2539-2549, Window 47 discussion of KIP-1262 where Kevin Wu provides detailed responses to Jun Rao's technical questions about the ClusterIdRecord implementation\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"index.md\\\",\\\"discussions.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests.md\\\",\\\"components.md\\\",\\\"issues.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":62.84,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":7,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":1082680,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":98077,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.326007,\\\"input_tokens\\\":170,\\\"output_tokens\\\":4283}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d512d18a-5d7d-4024-a813-727d525b922d","uuid":"8b311a6b-c394-4b3b-bf74-2546ea42664b","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:28:09.456Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Perfect! I found the answer. Based on the context filesystem, here's the answer to your question:\\\\n\\\\n## Answer\\